  "note": "η̂(−δ) = ∫₀^∞e^{−t²/2}e(δt)dt is the transform of the zero-extended weight (§9.2 sets η♥ = 0 for t < 0), not the √(2π)e^{−2π²δ²} of the remark after Thm 7.1.1. Lean states this shape only for two of its own weights, both extended by 0 to t ≤ 0."
